==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|frm|inimitable}}, from {{der|en|la|inimitabilis}}, corresponding to {{affix|en|in-|imitable}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɪnˈɪmɪtəbl̩/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-inimitable.oga|a=GA}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Beyond [[imitation]], [[surpass]]ing all others; [[matchless]].
#: {{antonyms|en|imitable|commonplace}}
#* {{RQ:Evelyn Numismata|page=201|passage=Moreover, a perfect ''Medal'' has its ''Profile'' and out-ſtroaks ſharp (''Nummus aſper'') and by no means rugged; the ''Figures'' clean and well poliſh'd; the ''Contours'' neatly trimm'd, and exactly round and carefully preſerv'd; that the Extancy and ''Relievos'' correſpond with the Ingraving, and have not ſuffer'd in ''Percuſſion''; in all which, there is a certain Spirit of Antiquity and Excellency to be diſcern'd in Antient ''Medals'' almoſt '''inimitable'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1947|author=w:Miriam Allen deFord|chapter=Laureate of Bohemia: George Sterlin|title=They Were San Franciscans|location=Caldwell, Idaho|publisher=The Caxton Printers, Ltd.|page=306|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/theyweresanfraci0000miri/page/306/mode/2up?q=inimitable|passage=Sterling himself, though he had the most picturesque and '''inimitable''' vocabulary of vituperation, was highly squeamish about ordinary smut or profanity. He had indeed that nice-Nelliness which is often characteristic of the Don Juan type.}}
#* {{quote-av|1=en|year=1959|author=|actor={{w|Martin Landau}}|role=Dan Hotaling|title={{w|The Twilight Zone (1959 TV series)|The Twilight Zone}}|episode={{w|Mr. Denton on Doomsday}}|season=1|number=3|time=1:34|text=Let's see you pay for your drink in your own '''inimitable''' fashion, huh? A song, Denton! How about it?}}

====Usage notes====
Not to be confused with {{m|en|inimicable|t=harmful, hostile}}.

